# File Deletion Approval

- Never delete a file unless I explicitly ask for that deletion in that message.
- Never infer approval to delete files from broad cleanup requests unless the files to delete are clearly identified and confirmed.
- If deletion seems useful, propose it first and wait for approval.
- Prefer moving or archiving files over deleting them when preservation may matter.
- If a task requires many deletions, summarize the planned deletions and ask for confirmation before proceeding.
